speechtext:
Going back to my hon. friend's first question I now have the information in regard to the composition of the committee. The original committee consisted of Hon. Robert Rogers, chairman, Hon. William Pugsley, Hon. J. D. Reid, Hon, J. D. Hazen, Hon. R. Lemieux, Hon. C. Murphy, Sir James Lougheed, Hon. P. E. Blondin and Hon. R. Watson. This committee was appointed in May, 1916. Mr. Murphy resigned on the 24th June, 1916. Hon. Mr. Lemieux resigned on September 1, 1916. Hon. Mr. Hazen having retired as Minister of Marine was replaced by Hon. C. C. Ballantyne, on October 24, 1917. Hon. Mr. Pugsley resigned on 23rd February, 1918. Hon. P. E. Blondin left for overseas military service on October 7, 1917. Hon. J. A. Calder and Hon. G. A. Robertson were nominated by Sir Robert Borden on March 25, 1919 to replace Hon. Messrs. Pugsley and Blondin respectively. Hon. J. A. Stewart and Hon. R. Monty were nominated by Right Hon. Arthur Meighen on September 22, 1921 to replace Hon. Dr. Reid and Hon. Mr. Calder elevated to the Senate. On September 25, 1921, the joint committee consisted of Hon. F. B. McCurdy, chairman;

Supply-Public Works
Hon. Mr. Ballantyne, Hon. Mr. Stewart, Hon. Mr. Monty, Sir James Lougheed, Hon. Mr. Robertson, and Hon. Mr. Watson.
